# Agent Content Sync

When you edit any site content (copy, features, partners, CLI commands, contest details), you **must also update** the three agent-facing files to keep them in sync:

## Files to update together

| Source change | Update these agent files |
|---|---|
| Feature copy (`Features.tsx`) | `public/llms.txt` → Features section, `public/index.html.md` → Features section, `AgentView.tsx` → `FEATURES` array |
| Partner data (`Partners.tsx`) | `public/llms.txt` → Ecosystem section, `public/index.html.md` → Ecosystem section, `AgentView.tsx` → `PARTNERS` array |
| CLI commands (`CliTerminal.tsx`) | `public/llms.txt` → CLI Commands section, `public/index.html.md` → CLI Reference table, `AgentView.tsx` → `CLI_COMMANDS` array |
| Contest details (`Desktop.tsx` `TreasureContent`) | `public/llms.txt` → Contest section, `public/index.html.md` → Contest section, `AgentView.tsx` → contest steps |
| Hero/tagline (`Hero.tsx`) | `public/llms.txt` → summary blockquote, `public/index.html.md` → intro, `index.html` → meta description |

## The three agent files

- `public/llms.txt` — Concise llmstxt.org-spec overview for LLMs fetching site info at inference time
- `public/index.html.md` — Full markdown mirror of the entire site for crawlers that don't execute JS
- `src/components/sections/AgentView.tsx` — In-app document view (shown when the user toggles "Agent" in the toolbar)

## Rule of thumb

If a human user would see different content after your edit, an agent should too. Update all three files.
